Inventory in mdj format (markdown with JSON). ais ignores this text, because
it is above the first level 1 heading.

- One level 1 heading for each role, system or product.
- Directly below the heading: one JSON block with the definitive values.
- "count" is the number of installs the entry stands for. Without it, an
  entry counts once. Hostname and IP are optional: give them when you want
  the device named in the alert, leave them out when the role is enough.
- Level 2 headings: free text. "## Usage" becomes the field "usage", and
  "## Interest" becomes the field "interest". The task's field policy
  decides what the model sees of each field.
- A product without a device record has no hostname and no ip. Without a
  version, every supported version is watched.
- Maintain the file with 'aisctl inventory' (list, set, add, rm, import),
  which never shows a real address.

# Internet edge firewalls

```json
{
  "vendor": "Palo Alto Networks",
  "product": "PAN-OS",
  "version": "11.1.4",
  "count": 2,
  "site": "earth"
}
```

## Usage

Edge firewalls, internet facing. No GlobalProtect VPN and no other services
on the internet facing interfaces. The management interface is firewall
protected.

## Interest

Only critical and high findings with an unauthenticated remote attack vector.

# vpn01.cyberdyne.systems

```json
{
  "hostname": "vpn01.cyberdyne.systems",
  "ip": "10.1.0.5",
  "site": "earth",
  "vendor": "Fortinet",
  "product": "FortiOS",
  "version": "7.4.5",
  "owner_email": "netops@cyberdyne.systems"
}
```

## Usage

SSL VPN gateway, internet facing. Authentication with SAML.

# Core switches

```json
{
  "vendor": "Cisco",
  "product": "IOS XE",
  "version": "17.9.5",
  "count": 4,
  "site": "venus"
}
```

## Usage

Core switches, internal only. The web UI is disabled. No SAML.

# app01.cyberdyne.systems

```json
{
  "hostname": "app01.cyberdyne.systems",
  "ip": "172.16.1.20",
  "site": "earth",
  "vendor": "Microsoft",
  "product": "Windows Server",
  "version": "2022",
